{"name":"Golden Touch","hex":"#caa444","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden touch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of Midas touch (“the ability to achieve financial reward (or, more generally, success) easily and consistently”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_touch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midas","blocks":[{"text":"Midas was a king of Phrygia with whom many myths became associated, as well as two later members of the Phrygian royal house."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Red-figure_stamnos_Silenos_Mida_440BC_Cropped.jpg/330px-Red-figure_stamnos_Silenos_Mida_440BC_Cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midas"},{"title":"Golden Touch (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Golden Touch\" is a song by English indie rock band Razorlight, appearing as the eighth track on their debut studio album, Up All Night (2004). The song is based on MTV2 and Queens of Noize DJ Mairead Nash, with whom Johnny Borrell had a brief relationship. \"Golden Touch\" was released as the fourth single from Up All Night in June 2004 and peaked at No. 9 on the UK Singles Chart. In 2006, it was ranked 87th on Q magazine's \"100 Greatest Songs Ever\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Golden_touch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Touch_(song)"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Red-figure_stamnos_Silenos_Mida_4